WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everyone.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.367
We're hanging out with
Will Smith right here!

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:08.467
I want to talk about
"King -- King Richard."

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.334
-"King Richard," yeah.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:12.367
-You're amazing in this movie,

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.167
and you're getting a lot of
good buzz on this.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:16.000
Congrats. Well deserved.
-Thank you.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.200
-But this is not the first time
you're playing a real person.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.434
-Yeah.
-Is that extra pressure?

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:25.434
-It is terrifying when you play
a real person

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:29.434
that is still alive and you know
that they're going to see it.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.567
You know?
-Yeah.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.067
-And it was beautiful.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:37.033
Venus and Serena were really
excited about the possibility.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:40.367
And they said that, you know,
they would potentially be

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.167
executive producers
and they would walk us

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.267
through the whole process,
but they were going to withhold

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:46.934
whether or not they put
their names on the film

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.334
until they saw it.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:51.234
So then I get the call that
Venus and Serena are walking

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:53.801
into the theater
to see the film.

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:56.234
And it's like --
it's the worst two hours ever.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.901
[ Laughter ]
It's the worst two hours.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.234
-"Please think I did
a good job."

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:02.634
-'Cause you spend so much time
creating these things

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:05.667
and there is literally only
one audience when you do it.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:08.701
I did it, you know,
with Muhammad Ali.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.100
And then with "Pursuit of
Happyness" and "Concussion"

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.167
with people that were all alive.
-Yes.

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:18.033
-And it's just --
it's the only audience.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:20.567
And you just hope to God that,
you know,

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.701
you've spent a year
to tell this story.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.968
-Doing the right thing.
-And you hope that they like it.

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:28.067
And Venus and Serena
cried all the way through

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:30.033
and they loved it.
-Loved it, yeah.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:33.667
One point that I heard
that they thought, like,

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.167
it looked and sounded
just like their dad.

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:36.234
-Their dad. Yeah, yeah.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.033
-That they were like,
"This is creepy."

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.968
It's like real.
"It's, like, freaking me out."

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:41.300
Like, "This is not real.
It's a movie."

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.000
-Yeah. What was really
interesting to me is that,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.701
you know, we all feel like
we have a picture of

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:49.133
Richard Williams,

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:54.334
and it's the classic overbearing
father hammering his children.

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:57.801
But in sitting with
Venus and Serena

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:00.367
and their sisters
and their mother,

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.767
it was completely the opposite.

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:09.501
He was a loving,
caring, doting father.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:12.868
Venus referred to it
as the Jedi mind trick,

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:19.033
that he had somehow made it
so they would have to ask him,

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:20.601
"Please, Daddy,
can we play tennis?"

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:23.901
Their punishment would be that
they couldn't play tennis

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:26.067
when they got in trouble.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:31.634
And it was -- You know, he
aligned with what they wanted

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.901
for themselves
more than demanding

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.200
what he wanted for them.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.367
-And it was a real lesson for me
as a parent, you know,

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:42.834
recognizing that you want to be
in alignment with your kids

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:45.133
versus forcing
and pushing and demanding.

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:46.667
-Telling them what to do, yeah.
-Telling them what to do.

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:51.100
It was a beautiful family story.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.601
It was beautiful.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:55.400
Here's Will Smith
in "King Richard."

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.734
Take a look at this.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:59.000
-I'm very confident.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.601
-You say it so easily.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.801
Why?

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.400
-Because I believe it.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.801
-But you haven't played a match
in almost three years.

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:10.267
-Alright, hold it right there,
if you don't mind.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:11.334
Let me tell you why.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:12.968
-Richard, we're doing
an interview.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:15.868
-What -- What she had said, she
said it with so much confidence

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:18.167
the first time,
but you keep going on and on.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.734
-But you can't just keep
interrupting if we're --

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:22.133
-What you got to understand is
you are dealing with the image

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:24.067
of a 14-year-old child.

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:26.767
And this child going to be
playing when your old ass and me

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.667
going to be in the grave.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:31.300
When she had said something, we
done told you what's happening.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.467
You are dealing with
a little black kid.

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:35.300
Let her be a kid.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.434
Now, she done answered it
with a lot of confidence.

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:38.801
Leave that alone!

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Whoa.

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.400
-That's how you do it!

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.534
Will Smith, everybody!

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:50.868
"King Richard" is in theaters
and streaming on HBO Max

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.234
starting next Friday.

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.300
And his book, "Will,"
is available now.

